            fork of Go's crypto/tls). The forked crypto/tls files retain
   their original BSD-3-Clause (The Go Authors) as noted in LICENSE-Go.
   Full MPL-2.0 text: https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/

2. github.com/XTLS/Xray-core (transport/internet/reality)
   Copyright XTLS
   License: Mozilla Public License 2.0 (MPL-2.0)
   Source: https://github.com/XTLS/Xray-core
   Used as: Reference for the lightweight Reality client port in
            hscontrol/xray/reality_client.go (UClient, VerifyPeerCertificate,
            SessionId/AEAD logic). That file is a clean-room Go port of the
            Xray-core logic and does not copy Xray-core's protobuf or
            framework code.

3. github.com/refraction-networking/utls v1.8.2
   Copyright The Go Authors and Refraction Networking contributors
   License: BSD 3-Clause (same terms as Go's crypto/tls) + MIT for the
